  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_bead9c9b139c485ba1fe016a77ba2c9d",
      "statement": "Each node holds a lease in the bucket and renews it after one third of the lifetime (CELLD_TTL_MS, default 10000 ms); a renewal that does not reach the bucket does not fence the node because it retries while the published expiry has not passed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L201-L206",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e62988dd3f881e42e2c110b15c1b050679ff492f7b4c499ee704afd19d1a2c97:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_031ffc8a3564446583f6c5f2c7fd02e9",
      "statement": "When its published expiry passes, a node fences itself: it stops each active cell and fails every uncompleted request, and a node whose lease record another writer replaced or removed fences at once; the fence writes nothing to the bucket.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L208-L218",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cc756212eeb2ae74a00b604b3d8e45c0a59f936ce33ae021781797d636ac980a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7d4711c613084dabb71e32619005da3f",
      "statement": "A fenced node logs a line starting with SELF-FENCE: and exits with code 3; the fenced state is terminal and only a restart returns the node to the fleet.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L220-L224",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:495eda4da1f964e9bfa6c07e6b530ee277989778d63c75e32bff130b5a1cd565:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a669220dd6274ac2a74c319c221fe06f",
      "statement": "The lease state machine lives in the decision core as NodeAuthority (Unstarted, Reading, Writing, Held, Retrying, Failed, Fenced), and a failed initial acquisition retries rather than leaving the node up with no authority for its whole lifetime.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L417-L443",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a35a3ad591a820b79d6e4f8f44c9ceebf9c73b939e4c41e226ee074df0f1e60c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53523ce9e7d24a51a67a20d04ac6b1b4",
      "statement": "celld must run under a supervisor that restarts the process without an attempt limit and waits at least one lease lifetime between attempts, so a repeated fence cycle is slow enough to observe.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L86-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:553bd90e457357c780b2a826cc1c25cb39952c3327d2eb6c0804fdf185f7c9ac:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1caea0bbba154e0388ec6ff6a8f5721e",
      "statement": "The first-readiness gate is pure logic in celld_logic::drain::fleet_status, which requires the node's own live lease, memory headroom on every live peer, a bounded restore backlog, and incumbent ownership within one equal successor share above the mean.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/drain.rs#L74-L153",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30e2c4a784d6d37e6266cadff5a789b464df40d32df2ce20d4a5b241417f64bd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71428e8b551846a5a424b307491df654",
      "statement": "A joining node can satisfy the ownership-skew condition when it advertises paced-handoff support and owns fewer cells than the busiest incumbent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/drain.rs#L52-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3927298e52194a0b1629dfe3314379ec6ab0283eed143cace2a2f94f6d000357:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b7ca9bebb3264ec0a945b74407102b44",
      "statement": "An unreadable fleet or an unsettled condition holds readiness for up to CELLD_READY_FLEET_GATE_MS (default 120000; 0 disables the gate), after which the process reports healthy with a ready_gate_expired event.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L489-L494",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9735f759f1364a6396df9af13736394d9f1cffa15c7c9eb971e100409133cbe6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e549af584ac74a71a4fa8fe5b668a8dd",
      "statement": "Graceful shutdown hands cells off in batches: the node proves a batch durable, publishes one full snapshot (an L9 object) of each closed database when the retry window allows, releases each ownership record, and asks a compatible peer to acquire it, keeping the cell dormant so the handoff does not restore an unused runtime.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L444-L456",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b59255e5498cdb2be10495df0ffe6b4a8a429e98feed50a639752220df576909:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a93152ea6e014ab29916f73bd75a6113",
      "statement": "Four settings pace the shutdown: CELLD_RELEASES (default 8) bounds complete handoffs in progress, CELLD_ACTIVATIONS limits restore and startup work, CELLD_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_MS (default 25000) sets the maximum interval without a completed handoff, and CELLD_SHUTDOWN_TOTAL_MS sets a 40000 ms default bound for the complete process stop.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L458-L468",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f49b41b33dd90d444f0990163e3780d9ea65ecca8cfa2c3b4915c398ed29bd8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_18965a1eef3643f5850bbb668484db2c",
      "statement": "The fleet drain token is one well-known bucket object at drain/token.json with a 120-second TTL.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/drain_token.rs#L18-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f936855181dc558a5e06469866eff2d35d1ac38f3306d357abea647a49873f37:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2394afe3ecfe49259b310af6f7d8ada2",
      "statement": "The drain token is advisory: correctness never depends on it, because a donor that cannot claim it within a bounded wait proceeds unserialized, a fresh node's gate falls open after a bounded wait, and a dead holder's claim lapses by TTL.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/drain.rs#L3-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5d61133333fc6ffe9952385cbffbbddbb57798fe78ff864bd1bdeeb747a432e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a480fc6849e4467baa41109139e9dfa7",
      "statement": "A donor that cannot claim the drain token within CELLD_DRAIN_TOKEN_WAIT_MS (default 30000; 0 disables the token) proceeds without it, and a handoff without the token is still safe.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L474-L477",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7bc6dbf2664cfa7c4774e2a2d2210138350796fd5625ba292cbc2cc4da002fdd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13327956482f4c6081e5b502d76dae49",
      "statement": "Dead-node GC retires historical node-cells/ index debris and expired node-session records, and the tombstone must carry the record's folded node-log field through unchanged because the lease record is the fleet log's root of truth.",
      "evidence": [
