    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cba87d33b58a4ebd88f22fc2cf3a0278",
      "statement": "The upgrade from v0.2.1 to v0.3.0 can use a rolling update, but a v0.3.0 node cannot replicate to a v0.2.x peer (so it acknowledges through the bucket), and a downgrade to v0.2.x can lose acknowledged writes unless the shutdown log contains node-log close: sealed epoch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L523-L534",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:158a48caf79168efb9b6643228ca827ca61d3217d16172d2d77d7fd7a72e3310:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_82d14936f23848a7afb41b9327a2316a",
      "statement": "The upgrade from v0.3.0 to v0.4.0 must not be a rolling update because v0.4.0 moves every proxied cell call onto one tunneled connection and the peer protocol refuses a different version, and v0.4.0 stores each new large KV value under its ownership epoch which a v0.3.0 node cannot read.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L535-L544",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09726a8f1fb6da7b2dc008054deb19c3ec50855d948e419804348e46563b02af:"
        }
      ]
    },
